   "pos": "RB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-16T22:03Z",
   "shortComment": "Johnson (hamstring) doesn't have an injury designation for Sunday's game at Las Vegas, Sam Warren of The Athletic reports.",
   "longComment": "Johnson was a new addition to the injury report this week, listed as limited Wednesday and Thursday before upgrading to full participation Friday. He made a big impact in the Week 5 win at Los Angeles, catching each of his four targets for 72 yards across just 14 snaps (21.9 percent snap share).",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "-2042674",
   "name": "Spencer Brown",
   "pos": "OT",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-16T00:30Z",
   "shortComment": "",
   "longComment": "",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642553",
   "name": "Landon Jackson",
   "pos": "DE",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-15T01:41Z",
   "shortComment": "Jackson (knee) was a full participant in Wednesday's walkthrough practice.",
   "longComment": "Jackson missed the Bills' Week 5 overtime win against the Rams due to a knee injury. The defensive end appears to have recovered from the injury after sitting out Week 5 and should be set to suit up for Sunday's game against the Raiders if he can continue to practice in full.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642391",
   "name": "Ray Davis",
   "pos": "RB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-14T02:57Z",
   "shortComment": "Davis caught his lone target for 31 yards while adding two carries for two yards and three kickoff returns for 114 yards during the Bills' 37-34 overtime win over the Rams on Monday.",
   "longComment": "Davis opened Monday's contest in style with a 70-yard return on the opening kickoff that set the Bills up deep in Rams territory, though the Rams defense forced a three-and-out and Buffalo had to settle for a 49-yard field goal. Davis made another big contribution early in the fourth quarter, when he turned a screen pass into a 31-yard gain before being tackled just short of the goal line, which led to a one-yard touchdown run by Josh Allen on the next play. Davis has been limited mostly to work on special teams while mixing in occasionally in the back field. That said, Davis and Ty Johnson could both be in the mix for more offensive touches, given that head coach Joe Brady said Tuesday that \"...at some point there has to be consequences\" in reference to James Cook's fumble issues this season, per Nick Suss of ESPN.com. The Bills will stay on the road for Week 6 against the Raiders on Oct. 18.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642343",
   "name": "Keon Coleman",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-13T23:25Z",
   "shortComment": "Coleman caught a seven-yard touchdown pass on two targets during the Bills' 37-34 overtime win over the Rams on Monday.",
   "longComment": "It was a statistically quiet night for Coleman despite the fact that DJ Moore (shoulder) was inactive, but Josh Allen completed only 12 of 19 passes and the Bills got most of their yardage on the ground. Coleman did have catches of 17 and seven yards in the third quarter negated by penalties, but the third-year pro was wide open for his touchdown after two Rams defensive backs collided. Coleman's 45 offensive snaps led all Bills wide receivers, and he has a 15-224-2 receiving line on 18 targets through five regular-season games. The Bills will stay on the road for Week 7 against the Raiders on Sunday, and Coleman's role on offense would shrink if Moore is cleared to return.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642300",
   "name": "Khalil Shakir",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-13T05:22Z",
   "shortComment": "Shakir brought in all three targets for 80 yards in the Bills' 37-34 overtime win over the Rams on Monday night.",
   "longComment": "On a night when Josh Allen completed just 12 passes, Shakir led the Bills in receiving yards with a figure that marked his second straight 80-yard-plus effort. However, Shakir needed overtime to get there, as he recorded a game-long 57-yard catch and run during Buffalo's first drive of the extra period. Shakir otherwise didn't see much benefit from the absences of DJ Moore and Joshua Palmer due to shoulder injuries, but he is now averaging an impressive 14.2 yards per catch heading into a Week 6 road matchup against the Raiders.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642294",
   "name": "Josh Allen",
   "pos": "QB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-13T04:50Z",
   "shortComment": "Allen completed 12 of 19 passes for 210 yards with one touchdown and one interception while adding 10 carries for 121 yards and another score and a two-point conversion pass in the Bills' 37-34 overtime win against the Rams on Monday night.",
   "longComment": "Facing a Rams defense that had forced plenty of inefficiency through the air from both wide receivers and tight ends and operating without both DJ Moore (shoulder) and Joshua Palmer (shoulder), Allen unsurprisingly recorded a season low in completions. However, the prolific signal-caller more than made up for it on the ground with a season-high rushing yardage total, as well as his eighth rushing touchdown of the season. Allen's most crucial runs outside of his one-yard scoring dive early in the fourth quarter came on Buffalo's final drive in overtime, when he rattled off 19- and 13-yard scrambles to move the ball from the Bills' 41-yard line to the Rams' 27-yard line to set up an eventual game-winning field goal from Tyler Bass. Allen also added his seventh passing score of the season late in the third quarter on a seven-yard strike to Keon Coleman, and the two-time All-Pro will next turn his sights to a Week 6 road matchup against the Raiders on Sunday.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "642292",
   "name": "James Cook III",
   "pos": "RB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-13T04:15Z",
   "shortComment": "Cook rushed 10 times for 121 yards and a touchdown and brought in his only target for seven yards in the Bills' 37-34 overtime win over the Rams on Monday night. He also committed two fumbles, losing one.",
   "longComment": "Cook put together another highly efficient night that saw him gain significant chunks of yards on multiple carries, and which featured his fifth rushing touchdown of the season on a 17-yard run in the later portion of the second quarter. However, Cook dodged what would have been a major blemish on his night -- a lost fumble at the Rams' 20-yard line in overtime -- when Josh Allen subsequently mounted a successful game-winning drive following a blocked field goal by Buffalo's special teams. Cook will take 532 rushing yards and an average of 5.6 yards per carry into a Week 6 road matchup against the Raiders on Sunday.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641808",
   "name": "Davison Igbinosun",
   "pos": "CB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-11T03:11Z",
   "shortComment": "Even with Christian Benford (toe) back from injury, Igbinosun is still expected to have a role in the Bills' secondary for Monday's game against the Rams, Nick Suss of ESPN.com reports.",
   "longComment": "Igbinosun made his first career start against the Patriots in Week 4 due to the absence of Benford, and the former finished with five tackles (three solo) and one pass defense while playing every single defensive snap. Benford and Maxwell Hairston will serve as Buffalo's starting outside cornerbacks Monday, but head coach Joe Brady is committed to having Igbinosun on the field on defense. The Bills' secondary will have its hands full against the lethal wideout duo of Puka Nacua and Davante Adams.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641756",
   "name": "Christian Benford",
   "pos": "CB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-10T19:17Z",
   "shortComment": "Benford (toe) does not carry an injury designation into Monday night's game against the Rams, Joe Buscaglia of The Athletic reports.",
   "longComment": "Benford has been given the green light to return from a one-game absence due to a toe injury that he sustained during the Bills' Week 3 win over the Chargers. He'll resume his starting spot at outside cornerback, and while rookie first-rounder Maxwell Hairston will start opposite Benford, rookie second-rounder Davison Igbinosun will also be involved in the Bills' secondary, per Nick Suss of ESPN.com.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641750",
   "name": "Skyler Bell",
   "pos": "WR",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-10T18:14Z",
   "shortComment": "Bell will make his NFL regular-season debut against the Rams on Monday due to the absence of Joshua Palmer (shoulder), Cameron Wolfe of NFL Network reports.",
   "longComment": "Bell has been a healthy scratch for each of the Bills' first four games of the regular season. However, he's expected to absorb Palmer's reps during Monday's game, and Bell could take on an even larger role if DJ Moore (shoulder) is also ruled out. Khalil Shakir, Keon Coleman and tight end Dalton Kincaid figure to be Josh Allen's go-to pass catchers if Moore cannot play, but Bell will at least be in the mix for targets in his NFL debut.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641337",
   "name": "Greg Rousseau",
   "pos": "LB",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-08T01:09Z",
   "shortComment": "Rousseau logged four tackles (two solo) and two passes defensed in the Bills' 29-26 loss to the Patriots on Sunday.",
   "longComment": "Rousseau notched 2.0 sacks in each of the first three games of the 2026 regular season. The outside linebacker's historic streak concluded in Week 4, when he was unable to log any sacks over 81 percent of the Bills' defensive snaps. The Bills' lack of defensive pressure against quarterback Drake Maye was a key component in the outcome of the early-season divisional matchup.",
   "details": null
  },
  {
   "id": "641019",
   "name": "Dawson Knox",
   "pos": "TE",
   "status": "Active",
   "date": "2026-10-06T02:41Z",
   "shortComment": "Knox caught both of his targets for 13 yards in the Bills' 29-26 loss to the Patriots on Sunday.",
   "longComment": "Knox was on the field frequently in 12-personnel packages during Sunday's contest but saw only two targets. The tight end likely will see the field more as the Bills lean back into 13-personnel packages to utilize Dalton Kincaid more in Week 5.",
   "details": null
  },
